          "title": "ED triage guidelines.pdf",
          "type": "file",
          "chunkId": "kch_amaraTri04",
          "locator": "§ 3.1",
          "quote": "Escalate any headache that is sudden and severe (\"thunderclap\"), or that comes with fever, neck stiffness, confusion, new weakness or changes in vision. These patients are graded 2 or higher and seen by a doctor without delay.",
          "score": 0.93
